### Model metrics in polar form

The model space of constant sectional curvature K and dimension n is the warped product metric `dr² + j_K(r)² · g_{S^{n-1}}` on `[0, R) × S^{n-1}` where `g_{S^{n-1}}` is the round metric on the unit sphere, and j_K solves `j'' + K j = 0`, `j(0) = 0`, `j'(0) = 1`.

A "metric" here is a bilinear form at each point: `g(v, w) = dr(v) dr(w) + j_K(r)² · g_S^{n-1}(π_*v, π_*w)` where v decomposes as (radial part, spherical part).

