The Laplacian comparison theorem (Wronskian route), stated cleanly:

```lean
theorem wronskian_nonneg {K₁ K₂ : ℝ} (hK : K₁ ≤ K₂) {r : ℝ} (hr : 0 ≤ r)
    (hfirst : 0 < K₂ → r ≤ Real.pi / Real.sqrt K₂) :
    0 ≤ jacobiDeriv K₁ r * jacobiSol K₂ r - jacobiSol K₁ r * jacobiDeriv K₂ r

theorem logDerivative_comparison {K₁ K₂ : ℝ} (hK : K₁ ≤ K₂) {r : ℝ} (hr : 0 < r)
    (hfirst : 0 < K₂ → r < Real.pi / Real.sqrt K₂) :
    jacobiDeriv K₂ r / jacobiSol K₂ r ≤ jacobiDeriv K₁ r / jacobiSol K₁ r

theorem laplacian_comparison (n : ℕ) {K₁ K₂ : ℝ} (hK : K₁ ≤ K₂) {r : ℝ} (hr : 0 < r)
    (hfirst : 0 < K₂ → r < Real.pi / Real.sqrt K₂) :
    radialLaplacian n (jacobiSol K₂) (fun x : ℝ => x) r ≤ radialLaplacian n (jacobiSol K₁) (fun x : ℝ => x) r := by
  rw [radialLaplacian_id n K₂ (ne_of_gt (jacobiSol_pos ...)), radialLaplacian_id n K₁ ...]
  exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (logDerivative_comparison hK hr hfirst) (Nat.cast_nonneg _)
```

and the "model value" formulation: `theorem laplacian_le_model (n) ... : radialLaplacian n (jacobiSol K₂) id r ≤ (n-1) * (jacobiDeriv K₁ r / jacobiSol K₁ r)`.

